## Pile of playing cards
// A drawable list:  each pile is its own element, e.g. <outline-solitaire-tableau>, which draws it in its own shadow root.
// So its styles are here, in its <css>, with those of the cards it draws:  styles.css can't reach in there.
a pile is a drawable list of cards
	- name is text
	// takes nothing:  a kind of pile says what it does take, e.g. a tableau
	- can never take a card
	- layout is one of stacked or vertical
	- color is:
		if it is empty return "none"
		return the color of its last card
	- value is:
		if it is empty return 0
		return the value of its last card
	- state is:
		set state to (the name of the pile or "pile") + ":"
		for each card in pile
			set state to state + " " + the state of the card
		return state
	<css>
		:host {
			display: block;
		}
		.Pile {
			position: relative;
			min-height: 30px;
		}
		.Pile.Tableau {
			min-height: 500px;
		}

		/* its layout:  stacked, the last card on top;  or vertical, each card below the one before */
		.Pile.stacked .Card {
			position: absolute;
			left: 0;
			right: 0;
			top: 0;
		}
		.Pile.vertical .Card {
			margin-bottom: 8px !important;
		}

		/* its cards */
		.Card {
			position: relative;
			height: 30px;
		}
		.Card .suit {
			position: relative;
			font-size: 1.5rem;
			padding-left: 1px;
			vertical-align: top;
			top: -0.15rem;
		}

		/* where a card goes when the pile is empty */
		.Pile > .Placeholder {
			position: relative;
			height: 30px;
		}
		.Pile > .Placeholder .suit {
			position: relative;
			font-size: 1.6rem;
		}
		.Pile > .Placeholder .suit.diamonds,
		.Pile > .Placeholder .suit.spades {
			font-size: 1.75rem;
			top: -0.1rem;
		}
	</css>

// a card is in one pile at a time:  putting it on another pile takes it off this one
a card belongs to one pile
